WEBVTT

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.900
<b>Miyagi High School Track and Field Meet</b>

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:10.360
The boys 5,000 meter finals will begin shortly.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:14.320
<b>Sendai Josei 
High School</b>

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.810
How's your stomach?

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:18.780
Hanging in there.

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:22.240
Sorry, but I won't hold back.

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:36.220
<b>Certain Victory</b>

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.000
You can do it, Kurahara!

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.210
Go!

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:53.190
<i>Apparently, he wasn't in perfect condition.</i>

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:55.690
<i>What? And he still finished in 13:54?</i>

00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:57.440
<i>Isn't he still a second-year?</i>

00:00:58.240 --> 00:00:59.780
Disgraceful!

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:03.790
Average times like these
are as good as losses!

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:05.620
Learn from Kurahara!

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:06.750
Yes, sir.

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:10.000
We're going back to the school
and running ten kilometers!

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.310
The next race has already begun!

00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:13.040
That's all!

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:15.050
Yes, sir.

00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:16.940
You don't need to run, Kurahara.

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:18.020
Good job.

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:18.720
Huh?

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:20.740
But...

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:22.860
Hurry it up, boys!

00:02:56.150 --> 00:03:00.030
<b><i>Run with the Wind</i></b>

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:04.480
It's been a while, Kurahara.

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:06.870
I was surprised.

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:09.630
I ran this course yesterday, too.

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:16.710
I didn't think you were still running.

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:20.000
Sakaki...

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:26.610
Who were those guys you were with?

00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:29.110
It's none of your business.

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:33.200
Really? Well, I guess it doesn't matter.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:35.470
Lucky you.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:37.820
You made some friends.

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:44.780
<b><i>Shadows That Don't Fade</i></b>

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:50.660
When you analyze this statistical data...

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:10.470
<b>Pachinko Comeback</b>

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:24.780
<b>Nanapan</b>

00:04:36.730 --> 00:04:38.040
What are you doing?

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:43.130
Is that all you can do?

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:45.090
Is it?

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:50.310
Kurahara.

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:54.480
What's wrong? You're spacing out.

00:04:55.090 --> 00:04:56.800
It's nothing.

00:04:57.310 --> 00:04:58.920
He's an underclassman at my dorm.

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:03.900
<b>Udon/Soba</b>

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:03.900
<b>Ramen</b>

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:03.900
<b>Curry Menu                Plated Dishes 

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:07.320
You're wrong!

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:08.950
That's a shallow interpretation!

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:11.730
But the protagonist said so himself.

00:05:11.730 --> 00:05:12.910
He can't take it anymore.

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:16.580
You're missing the panel that comes after that!

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:18.980
The author hasn't given up!

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:21.750
You should go home right now
and see for yourself!

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:23.210
Passionate, right?

00:05:23.610 --> 00:05:26.930
We're always like this when it comes to comics.

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:29.180
It wouldn't be an exaggeration to say

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:32.310
everything important we've learned
about life has come from comics.

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:35.380
Friendship, hard work, and everything else.

00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:36.890
It's an enriching experience.

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:38.980
Why don't you join us?

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:41.050
The Comics Club welcomes you.

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:45.190
Why don't you begin 
your new college life with us?

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:48.130
But I don't read comics...

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:51.150
Sir, we'll clear a table for you.

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:03.340
No king rules forever.

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:06.110
What you really need
is intellect and sensibility.

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:10.790
Huh? Isn't that Prince and the newbie?

00:06:10.790 --> 00:06:11.590
What?

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:13.980
Did he join the Comics Club?

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:15.270
Whatever.

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:20.440
So, is Shindo serious
about continuing practice?

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:23.110
At the very least, 
his expression seemed earnest.

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:26.140
On top of that, on the way back from jogging,

00:06:26.140 --> 00:06:30.110
I saw Haiji and Shindo whispering
to each other about club dues.

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:36.080
When I looked up "club
dues" in the dictionary...

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:36.790
It's money.

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:40.160
Yes! They're talking about money.

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:44.970
What am I going to do if 
they request money from me?

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:47.260
So you know the word for "request"...

00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:49.960
The training is hard enough.

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:51.740
I can't give them money...

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:53.040
Damn.

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:57.860
As long as it was just Haiji who was
excited about it, we could easily ignore it.

00:06:57.860 --> 00:06:59.990
The twins are already on board.

00:06:59.990 --> 00:07:03.400
If he convinces two more people,
the yeses will have the majority.

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:08.740
See you at Aotake.

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:16.910
By the way, did anyone buy the newest volume?

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:19.460
Who were they?

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:23.380
Those guys you were with.

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:25.840
It's none of your business.

00:07:26.690 --> 00:07:29.910
Really? Well, I guess it doesn't matter.

00:07:30.970 --> 00:07:32.200
Lucky you.

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:34.720
You made some friends.

00:07:42.890 --> 00:07:44.860
<b>Everyone's Forest</b>

00:07:55.180 --> 00:07:57.280
You can do it, Kurahara!

00:07:57.280 --> 00:07:59.790
It's the home stretch!

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:02.040
Go!

00:08:03.350 --> 00:08:08.390
I didn't think you were still running.

00:08:08.390 --> 00:08:09.300
Shut up.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:12.300
Wait! Thief!

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:16.260
Who were those guys you were with?

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:18.350
<i>Why?</i>

00:08:18.670 --> 00:08:20.530
<i>Why couldn't I say anything?</i>

00:08:20.530 --> 00:08:22.140
<i>Why?</i>

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:24.020
What are you afraid of?

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:25.380
You're fast.

00:08:27.230 --> 00:08:28.960
I'm not scared!

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:31.680
Who cares? Run with us.

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:32.490
I can't!

00:08:34.260 --> 00:08:35.260
Hey!

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:36.910
You like running?

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:40.370
Do you like running?

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:42.630
Don't...

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:44.260
Don't ask me that!

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:00.580
Cold!

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:03.130
Sorry.

00:09:03.130 --> 00:09:05.000
Really, I'm fine.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:08.050
If anything, I'm glad you weren't hurt.

00:09:08.050 --> 00:09:09.190
Don't.

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:11.230
You're an important athlete.

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:15.400
Haiji said God might exist, after all.

00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:21.190
After meeting you, he said,
"We're no ordinary men."

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:23.370
"We're destined for something great."

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:28.700
He wouldn't stop talking
about running together.

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:30.920
There.

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:37.260
The only thing I understand
is that you're really, really fast.

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:42.560
That's all.

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:46.980
I can't do anything but run.

00:09:49.850 --> 00:09:50.880
Hey!

00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:07.460
I know. Wanna race?

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:08.270
Huh?

00:10:08.270 --> 00:10:10.870
Let's race to Aotake with Nira.

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:12.240
Okay.

00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:14.570
Ready...

00:10:14.570 --> 00:10:15.340
Why?

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:17.780
Why won't you leave me alone?

00:10:18.270 --> 00:10:22.260
If you want to run, you can run by yourself.

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:25.660
Isn't that what it means to run?

00:10:26.790 --> 00:10:29.170
I'm sorry, but you should give up on me.

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:32.640
I—

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:33.670
Kurahara.

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:39.280
Even though you run by yourself,
you're not actually alone.

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:46.600
You're always running with someone else.

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:51.580
I don't understand.

00:10:55.030 --> 00:10:55.910
I see.

00:10:56.650 --> 00:10:57.810
Okay, Nira.

00:10:57.810 --> 00:10:59.840
Ready... go!

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:02.720
You're fast, Nira.

00:11:07.280 --> 00:11:08.550
Someone?

00:11:17.130 --> 00:11:18.390
You bought shoes?

00:11:18.390 --> 00:11:21.520
Yeah. Specialized shoes are better, apparently.

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:25.970
Your attendance has been perfect.

00:11:25.970 --> 00:11:27.850
So, what?

00:11:27.850 --> 00:11:29.090
Nothing.

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:31.370
Everyone's here.

00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:34.310
Hana's waiting for us at the finish line today.

00:11:34.310 --> 00:11:35.180
What?

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:41.050
<b>Feeble</b>

00:11:36.390 --> 00:11:38.750
Hana will be timing us today.

00:11:38.750 --> 00:11:41.050
Do whatever it takes to finish.

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:43.360
Kurahara, you, too.

00:11:44.130 --> 00:11:46.270
If we don't all get there,

00:11:46.270 --> 00:11:51.720
Hana will be waiting at the 
Tamagawa River forever and ever.

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:55.400
I've told her we're starting at exactly six.

00:11:56.290 --> 00:11:57.860
30 seconds to go.

00:11:57.860 --> 00:11:59.100
All right!

00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:01.050
We'll show you what we can do!

00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:03.990
Then you guys should get new shoes.

00:12:03.990 --> 00:12:05.270
Aren't those basketball shoes?

00:12:05.270 --> 00:12:07.330
Huh? What do you mean?

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:10.290
I'll take you someplace special sometime.

00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:13.120
Why does that sound so indecent?

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:14.250
I can't take it!

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:16.730
See? He's trying to win them over.

00:12:16.730 --> 00:12:20.090
Calm down. The twins have
always been on his side.

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:22.920
Eight, seven, six,

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:24.450
Good grief.

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:28.140
five, four, three, two, one.

00:12:24.870 --> 00:12:26.640
What a waste of time.

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:29.060
Go!

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:38.880
How is he so fast?

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:39.940
It's infuriating!

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:42.250
Don't get thrown off by his pace!

00:12:42.250 --> 00:12:43.650
Same thing goes for races!

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:45.360
Got it!

00:12:46.140 --> 00:12:49.780
Prince, I'm extremely moved right now.

00:12:49.780 --> 00:12:51.080
By what?

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:55.540
In just one week, your pace
has increased substantially.

00:12:55.860 --> 00:12:58.320
You have that much aptitude.

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:05.860
Do it, and you'll understand.

00:13:05.860 --> 00:13:07.690
Never do it, and you'll never understand.

00:13:08.020 --> 00:13:09.850
That's from "The Burning Pen"—

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:14.540
Comics taught you 
everything that matters, right?

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:19.980
Hey! Over here!

00:13:20.330 --> 00:13:22.500
Oh, wow! You're so fast!

00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:24.440
Ah, to be young.

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:27.030
Please stop.

00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:28.620
Goal!

00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:31.580
Wow! 14:53.

00:13:32.030 --> 00:13:34.280
Five kilometers in 14:53?

00:13:34.280 --> 00:13:35.080
That's fast.

00:13:36.060 --> 00:13:38.500
You holding back, Kurahara?

00:13:39.100 --> 00:13:41.460
Five kilometers in 14:53?

00:13:41.990 --> 00:13:45.170
That time would've been
unthinkable for you in high school.

00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:46.630
Who are you?

00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:51.180
I'm Tokyo Sport University
first-year Sakaki Kosuke.

00:13:51.630 --> 00:13:53.490
Who are you? The manager?

00:13:53.490 --> 00:13:56.100
I'm not the manager, but...

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:59.690
She's timing us. We're busy.

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:01.020
Timing you?

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:02.900
But no one's coming.

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:06.680
Oh, I get it. So that's how it is.

00:14:06.680 --> 00:14:11.990
Even you lower your level when
running with such low-level guys.

00:14:13.210 --> 00:14:16.080
I finally understood after contacting the OBs.

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:19.100
They said you're attending Kansei University.

00:14:19.100 --> 00:14:21.120
Do they even have a track and field team?

00:14:22.010 --> 00:14:24.800
Is this some kind of friendly jogging club?

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:25.760
Just go!

00:14:29.670 --> 00:14:31.870
You going to hit me again?

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:33.310
What?

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:35.770
Yeah!

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:42.230
You really should get new shoes.

00:14:42.230 --> 00:14:44.160
It's way easier, Musa.

00:14:45.210 --> 00:14:49.170
Your time's improving.

00:14:49.170 --> 00:14:51.710
So, what?

00:14:51.710 --> 00:14:55.790
That's odd. Maybe it's because
there was a headwind today.

00:14:55.790 --> 00:14:57.850
Then you'd all be running
under the same circumstances.

00:14:57.850 --> 00:14:58.660
Right.

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:04.840
Who's that guy?

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:06.550
Look, Prince!

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:10.140
Your friends are waiting for you!
The heroes of Aotake!

00:15:10.140 --> 00:15:14.910
They're waiting for the warrior
named Prince to return!

00:15:15.370 --> 00:15:18.200
Sounds like something Prince would enjoy.

00:15:18.200 --> 00:15:20.350
Haiji's learning.

00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:21.370
That's right!

00:15:21.370 --> 00:15:26.400
Today, you'll reach an unknown
territory you've never reached before!

00:15:29.980 --> 00:15:31.910
You're here!

00:15:43.110 --> 00:15:45.980
34:59:28.

00:15:48.140 --> 00:15:50.600
Hear that, Prince? 34 minutes.

00:15:50.600 --> 00:15:54.150
You broke the 35-minute wall. You did it.

00:15:58.730 --> 00:16:00.600
What is this? A seniors marathon?

00:16:01.780 --> 00:16:03.520
I can walk faster than that.

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:09.400
What?

00:16:11.810 --> 00:16:14.380
You know each other? Where are you from?

00:16:14.380 --> 00:16:17.100
Excuse me, Coach. I'm—

00:16:17.100 --> 00:16:18.200
I'm not the coach.

00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:20.080
I'm a fourth-year. An athlete.

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:23.790
Excuse me. I know Kurahara.

00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:27.490
He really helped me out a lot in high school.

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:29.740
You're on the track and field team?

00:16:29.740 --> 00:16:31.940
Yes, on Tokyo Sports Uni's.

00:16:32.290 --> 00:16:33.810
Tokyo Sports Uni...

00:16:33.810 --> 00:16:36.380
Then we'll see you at the track meet.

00:16:36.380 --> 00:16:37.350
Track meet?

00:16:37.750 --> 00:16:41.550
The Tokyo Sports Uni track
meet is at the end of the month.

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:43.060
Yes, but...

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:44.810
Then we'll see you there.

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:47.860
Isn't that enough?

00:16:47.860 --> 00:16:51.210
What? You're going to run at the track meet?

00:16:51.210 --> 00:16:54.820
Of course. We can't qualify
without official records.

00:16:55.150 --> 00:16:56.780
Haiji, stop!

00:16:57.440 --> 00:16:58.620
Qualify?

00:16:58.620 --> 00:16:59.620
Don't!

00:17:00.350 --> 00:17:02.040
For the Hakone Ekiden.

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:10.350
What?

00:17:11.290 --> 00:17:15.610
To participate in the Hakone Ekiden
qualifier, we need official records.

00:17:15.610 --> 00:17:17.810
So we'll run at the meet.

00:17:17.810 --> 00:17:19.390
All of us.

00:17:20.190 --> 00:17:23.760
Those ten guys are the Kansei
University Hakone Ekiden team.

00:17:26.690 --> 00:17:29.680
Hakone? Is he serious?

00:17:30.680 --> 00:17:33.820
Are you making light of track and field? Huh?

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:35.170
No.

00:17:35.170 --> 00:17:37.280
I'm asking you, Kurahara!

00:17:41.450 --> 00:17:42.870
What is that?

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:45.770
Don't worry.

00:17:45.770 --> 00:17:47.290
If anything happens...

00:17:49.190 --> 00:17:50.310
Whoa...

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:52.990
Say something.

00:17:53.370 --> 00:17:56.690
Aren't you embarrassed to run at their level?

00:17:56.690 --> 00:17:58.130
Our level?

00:18:00.550 --> 00:18:03.010
If anything, I find it invigorating.

00:18:09.120 --> 00:18:11.400
This is why I hate them...

00:18:13.140 --> 00:18:16.420
It's always about levels, winning and losing.

00:18:16.420 --> 00:18:19.110
They can only describe things on that level.

00:18:20.090 --> 00:18:21.450
Prince?

00:18:22.070 --> 00:18:25.430
I really hate running,

00:18:25.950 --> 00:18:27.250
but more than that,

00:18:27.250 --> 00:18:33.290
I hate people who criticize
others for what they do!

00:18:36.610 --> 00:18:39.970
I'm not sure if these people
are my friends or not.

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:40.900
Hey.

00:18:41.290 --> 00:18:42.430
But at the very least,

00:18:42.430 --> 00:18:50.060
they recognize me, my ideas, and my worth.

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:54.150
Among them, there is no high or low level.

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:58.610
The only thing that matters is who we are!

00:19:00.270 --> 00:19:01.070
So I...

00:19:05.300 --> 00:19:06.440
Prince...

00:19:07.420 --> 00:19:08.250
You heard him.

00:19:08.720 --> 00:19:10.710
That was quick!

00:19:13.080 --> 00:19:15.170
Kakeru will get faster.

00:19:15.690 --> 00:19:18.860
Even faster than when you knew him.

00:19:32.460 --> 00:19:33.310
Sakaki!

00:19:39.370 --> 00:19:40.450
We'll meet again.

00:19:48.920 --> 00:19:51.520
What was that? A declaration of war?

00:19:51.520 --> 00:19:52.490
What?

00:19:52.490 --> 00:19:54.740
Didn't you mean he'll pay for this?

00:19:54.740 --> 00:19:56.040
No!

00:19:56.040 --> 00:19:58.200
You're the type to provoke 
people subconsciously.

00:19:58.200 --> 00:19:58.920
What?!

00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:00.540
You were cool, though.

00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:03.080
You, Haiji, and Prince.

00:20:03.080 --> 00:20:05.010
We've got a goal for now.

00:20:06.380 --> 00:20:08.930
Yeah! Let's run in this track meet!

00:20:08.930 --> 00:20:11.980
You just watch us, damn it!
Who cares if we're low level?

00:20:13.130 --> 00:20:15.750
Prince is right. You're you.

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:18.370
Do what you want.

00:20:18.370 --> 00:20:19.830
So will I.

00:20:21.190 --> 00:20:27.160
That's why I'll run with you
and the rest of the guys.

00:20:33.140 --> 00:20:36.440
Let's head back. Breakfast is waiting.

00:20:36.440 --> 00:20:38.630
Yeah!

00:20:40.970 --> 00:20:43.270
Can you walk?

00:20:41.170 --> 00:20:43.270
Finally, food!

00:20:43.270 --> 00:20:45.980
This is the beginning of our adventure!

00:22:40.670 --> 00:22:43.380
Next time: "The Ones Not Chosen."

00:22:41.630 --> 00:22:46.000
<b>Next Time: The Ones Not Chosen</b>
